          {
            "commit": "980e1e28999a485c6accaa9ee29ebd31bcf9a0a0",
            "subject": "LU-9868 llite: use d_splice_alias for directories."
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-07 16:36:08.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-07 16:36:16.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-9868 tests: rename through a stale directory dentry",
        "message": "LU-9868 tests: rename through a stale directory dentry\n\nA client that gives a directory inode a second hashed dentry\ncan make rename(2) take that directory's i_rwsem twice and\nhang in D state, which was seen as racer test_2 hangs:\nlock_rename() and its loop check compare dentries, so they\ntake the two dentries for different directories.\n\nAdd sanityn test_123 to form the second dentry on purpose.\nThe first mount holds its cwd in foo/bar, which keeps foo\nand foo/bar hashed after the second mount moves bar out of\nfoo and then foo under bar. A rename of ../baz onto foo from\nthat cwd then reaches the source through the stale foo\ndentry, since \"..\" is not revalidated, and looks up foo\nunder bar, where the client used to add a second dentry for\nfoo.\nThe rename runs in the background and the test fails if it\nhas not returned after 30 seconds.\n\nWithout the d_splice_alias() change for directories the\nrename hangs in vfs_rename(); with it the lookup of foo\nfails with ELOOP and the rename returns.\n\nBased on the reproducer in https://review.whamcloud.com/65122\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=123,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iabbdfe02d79db0b3bcbcc1e1adebf0645ad921bc\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
